        {
          "type": "tool_result",
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_014yedkSau26BVBMZssJQCaK",
          "content": "{\"as_of_date\": \"2026-02-10\", \"clauses\": [{\"clause_id\": \"POL-MTR-002:3.4\", \"version\": \"5.3\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"effective_from\": \"2025-03-01\", \"effective_to\": \"2026-03-01\", \"document_review_date\": \"2026-03-01\", \"text\": \"POL-MTR-002 Motor Vehicle Coverage and Exclusions (v5.3, SUPERSEDED: applies to incidents before 2026-03-01) > 3. Exclusions > 3.4 Unlicensed driving \\u2014 ABSOLUTE\\nNo cover where the driver was unlicensed, disqualified, or driving outside\\nlicence conditions at the time of the incident. A licence that had expired, for\\nany period, is treated as no licence. No rebuttal is available.\"}, {\"clause_id\": \"POL-MTR-002:3.2\", \"version\": \"5.3\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"effective_from\": \"2025-03-01\", \"effective_to\": \"2026-03-01\", \"document_review_date\": \"2026-03-01\", \"text\": \"POL-MTR-002 Motor Vehicle Coverage and Exclusions (v5.3, SUPERSEDED: applies to incidents before 2026-03-01) > 3. Exclusions > 3.2 Intoxication \\u2014 ABSOLUTE\\nNo cover where the driver's blood alcohol concentration at the time of the\\nincident exceeded **0.05 g/100mL**, or exceeded 0.00 where the driver held a\\nlearner, provisional or probationary licence. Confirmed by police breath or\\nblood analysis.\"}, {\"clause_id\": \"POL-MTR-002:3.5\", \"version\": \"5.3\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"effective_from\": \"2025-03-01\", \"effective_to\": \"2026-03-01\", \"document_review_date\": \"2026-03-01\", \"text\": \"POL-MTR-002 Motor Vehicle Coverage and Exclusions (v5.3, SUPERSEDED: applies to incidents before 2026-03-01) > 3. Exclusions > 3.5 Unlisted driver \\u2014 REBUTTABLE\\nWhere the policy names specific drivers, no cover applies if the vehicle was\\ndriven by a person not listed.\\n**Rebuttal condition**: cover may be restored on payment of an additional\\nexcess of **AUD 2,000** where the driver was aged 25 or over, held a full\\nlicence for 2 or more years, and had the insured's permission.\"}, {\"clause_id\": \"POL-MTR-002:3.15\", \"version\": \"5.3\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"effective_from\": \"2025-03-01\", \"effective_to\": \"2026-03-01\", \"document_review_date\": \"2026-03-01\", \"text\": \"POL-MTR-002 Motor Vehicle Coverage and Exclusions (v5.3, SUPERSEDED: applies to incidents before 2026-03-01) > 3. Exclusions > 3.15 Recently lapsed registration \\u2014 REBUTTABLE\\nWhere registration had expired by **14 days or less** at the incident date,\\ncover may be restored where registration was renewed within 14 days of the\\nincident and the vehicle was otherwise roadworthy.\"}, {\"clause_id\": \"POL-MTR-002:3.6\", \"version\": \"5.3\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"effective_from\": \"2025-03-01\", \"effective_to\": \"2026-03-01\", \"document_review_date\": \"2026-03-01\", \"text\": \"POL-MTR-002 Motor Vehicle Coverage and Exclusions (v5.3, SUPERSEDED: applies to incidents before 2026-03-01) > 3. Exclusions > 3.6 Young or inexperienced driver excess\\nNot an exclusion but a loading. Where the driver at the incident date was under\\n**25 years of age**, or held a full licence for less than 2 years, an\\nadditional excess of **AUD 1,200** applies per POL-STL-007 clause 3.4.\"}, {\"clause_id\": \"POL-MTR-002:3.14\", \"version\": \"5.3\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"effective_from\": \"2025-03-01\", \"effective_to\": \"2026-03-01\", \"document_review_date\": \"2026-03-01\", \"text\": \"POL-MTR-002 Motor Vehicle Coverage and Exclusions (v5.3, SUPERSEDED: applies to incidents before 2026-03-01) > 3. Exclusions > 3.14 Unregistered or unroadworthy \\u2014 ABSOLUTE\\nNo cover where the vehicle was unregistered at the incident date, or where a\\ndefect notice was in force and unremedied and that defect contributed to the\\nincident. Registration expired by 14 days or less is treated under clause 3.15.\"}, {\"clause_id\": \"POL-MTR-002:3.8\", \"version\": \"5.3\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"effective_from\": \"2025-03-01\", \"effective_to\": \"2026-03-01\", \"document_review_date\": \"2026-03-01\", \"text\": \"POL-MTR-002 Motor Vehicle Coverage and Exclusions (v5.3, SUPERSEDED: applies to incidents before 2026-03-01) > 3. Exclusions > 3.8 Racing and testing \\u2014 ABSOLUTE\\nNo cover for damage sustained during racing, time trials, speed testing,\\ntrack days, or driver-training events held on a closed circuit.\"}, {\"clause_id\": \"POL-MTR-002:3.9\", \"version\": \"5.3\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"effective_from\": \"2025-03-01\", \"effective_to\": \"2026-03-01\", \"document_review_date\": \"2026-03-01\", \"text\": \"POL-MTR-002 Motor Vehicle Coverage and Exclusions (v5.3, SUPERSEDED: applies to incidents before 2026-03-01) > 3. Exclusions > 3.9 Flood and water \\u2014 REBUTTABLE\\nNo cover for damage caused by driving into floodwater where the water depth was\\nvisible or signage prohibited entry.\\n**Rebuttal condition**: cover may be restored where the vehicle was stationary\\nand parked at the time of inundation, or where the driver entered the water in\\nresponse to a direction by emergency services.\"}], \"note\": \"Cite the clause_ids you rely on. If none of these answers the question, say the policy library doesn't cover it.\"}",
